name  = axpy
shape = c[i] = c[i] + alpha * a[i] over two float Vecs, 20 passes, 2,000,000 elements
args  = 2000000
cflags = -ffp-contract=off
claim = the row that forced range-check versioning (Q-108). With a bounds check
        per element the loop has three early exits and clang leaves it scalar:
        2.8x hand-written C at v0.1.415. With the whole index range checked once
        before the loop (v0.1.420) clang vectorizes it and the expectation is a
        TIE with C. Memory-bound at this size, so SIMD itself is worth about 1.3x
        here; the check's shape was the rest of the gap, which is the point the
        row exists to make. Same LCG, unfused arithmetic and bit-pattern output
        as matmul, and for the same reasons (see its MANIFEST).

# 36,700,448 B at v0.1.420: two 2,000,000-element float Vecs built by vec_push
# (16 MiB each once grown) plus the growth steps. Nothing else allocates: the
# passes mutate in place. A reading above the ceiling means a pass started
# allocating; below the floor means the meter stopped seeing the Vecs.
alloc_min = 33554432
alloc_max = 50331648
